implementationPlan.description:
ADVERSARIAL SELF-REVIEW of this task's own diff, the last step (load adversarial-self-review). This task is epic-final only by the highest-order fallback: epic-be924fb8 has no finalTaskId and every sibling had its own QA. So also re-read how this diff meets a2f243a1 and dfbda1a8 (Get-MoeRecordHeldFields sends) and f943b687 (getCommitScope.ts, and recordCommit.ts CONTESTED_EDITING_RE). Check and note each item:

(1) Only adds holds. No path that HEAD's wrapper landed under skip, commit or declare_files changes fate unless a peer is mid-step on it. Diff every branch of the contested block in both wrappers.

(2) Legacy parity. A scope without taskIds or editingTaskIds, or a hand-built ps1 entry @{Path;TaskId}, gives exactly today's candidates, skips, contested rows, trailers and held= text. AK3, importee-guard.ps1 and importee-guard-bash.test.mjs show it.

(3) Error handling. Feed each parser junk by hand:
- null entries;
- taskIds as a string or a number;
- editingTaskIds with a null element;
- a peer record whose implementationPlan is an object;
- a step whose affectedFiles is a string.
No exception may reach the landing, and the disk fallback must never degrade to the empty last-resort scope.

(4) PowerShell list handling:
- one-element and empty lists in the RPC parse are read raw;
- no `@($null)` row or empty-id hold is possible.

(5) Trailers group exactly one path per line. Rows of different paths are never merged, and one path's rows are never split. The ids appear in taskIds order with the entry's taskId first.

(6) The editing code carries a task id that record_commit's CONTESTED_EDITING_RE (task-[A-Za-z0-9_-]+) accepts. A malformed id still holds the path; it only raises no alert.

(7) Disk fallback:
- DONE and ARCHIVED records are still skipped;
- editing only marks paths the task contributes;
- fails closed with no activity data.

(8) EDIT, UNTOUCHED and NEVER are byte-identical across the 2 wrappers and 2 harnesses. Parity checks are green, and moe-agent.ps1 still has its BOM.

(9) Two landings at once: the attribution is still a pure function of scope plus snapshot, with no new shared state.

(10) The docs agree with docs/MCP_SERVER.md.

In the completion summary, report:
- the net non-board LOC, which must be under 400;
- whether each doc was clean before its edit, and the carrying sha if a peer's landing took a doc hunk;
- the AK RED/GREEN evidence;
- the snapshot gate result.
